# Firewall of broker node rabbit2 (data 172.28.3.62).
# Clients (booking, notifier) use port 5672. The three nodes talk to each
# other on 4369 (node lookup) and 25672 (cluster traffic).
# Its web console is published on 127.0.0.1:15673 of the laptop, so the
# cluster can still be looked at when rabbit1 is down.
# direction  peer          port   rule name
in           172.28.3.20   5672   booking-to-rabbit2
in           172.28.3.30   5672   notifier-to-rabbit2
in           172.28.3.1    15672  laptop-to-rabbit2-console
in           172.28.3.61   4369   rabbit1-to-rabbit2-lookup
in           172.28.3.61   25672  rabbit1-to-rabbit2-cluster
in           172.28.3.63   4369   rabbit3-to-rabbit2-lookup
in           172.28.3.63   25672  rabbit3-to-rabbit2-cluster
out          172.28.3.61   4369   rabbit2-to-rabbit1-lookup
out          172.28.3.61   25672  rabbit2-to-rabbit1-cluster
out          172.28.3.63   4369   rabbit2-to-rabbit3-lookup
out          172.28.3.63   25672  rabbit2-to-rabbit3-cluster
# Command-line tools (rabbitmqctl) on one node collect answers from the
# other nodes on ports 35672-35682.
in           172.28.3.61   35672:35682  rabbit1-to-rabbit2-cli
out          172.28.3.61   35672:35682  rabbit2-to-rabbit1-cli
in           172.28.3.63   35672:35682  rabbit3-to-rabbit2-cli
out          172.28.3.63   35672:35682  rabbit2-to-rabbit3-cli
